@page "/account/denied"

<PageTitle>Access denied · LOS/LMS</PageTitle>

@* Where the cookie handler sends a signed-in user who fails a role check.

   It used to send them to the sign-in page, which is actively misleading: they ARE signed in, and
   being shown a login form suggests their session expired rather than that they lack the role. *@

<div class="auth-page">
    <div class="auth-card">
        <div class="auth-head">
            <span class="auth-system">LOS/LMS</span>
            <h1 class="auth-title">Access denied</h1>
            <p class="auth-sub">
                Your account does not have permission to open that page. Company Setup and the Admin
                Inbox are restricted to Admin and SuperAdmin users — ask an administrator if you need
                access.
            </p>
        </div>

        <a class="auth-secondary" href="/applications">← Back to applications</a>
    </div>
</div>
